# The finite literal triple-wave expansion

The polar formula for the pair kernel contains three spherical Fourier
factors.  The two coordinate normal-form files express each factor as the
sum of its outgoing endpoint, incoming endpoint, and middle contribution.
This file performs that expansion once and for all as an explicit finite
sum.  In particular, the later cone argument estimates the twenty-seven
literal summands of the actual kernel; it is not an invocation of an
abstract stationary-kernel hypothesis.

